<urn:atm:triage:finding/AN6-RULE008-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AN6-RULE008-003" ;
  triage:title "Raw production identity literal 'atm-dev' in atm-query-python lib.rs test" ;
  triage:description "AN6-QA-4 (quality-mgr) independent re-verification of AN6-RULE008-002 confirmed that fix genuinely closed, but surfaced a separate, pre-existing RULE-008/009 violation not caught during AN6-QA-3: crates/atm-query-python/src/lib.rs:179, in test parameterized_query_returns_column_labelled_rows, uses PyTuple::new(py, [raw literal atm-dev]) as a query parameter. This literal predates AN6QA2-FIX-1 (present unchanged at 59ee84654 and still at 77acf6a0a); confirmed via git diff 59ee84654..77acf6a0a --stat showing only templates.rs changed. Recommend replacing the raw literal with the same TEST_* fixture pattern used for templates.rs (e.g. a shared test-identity constant). This finding blocks just lint identities check / PR #862 mergeability." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-an" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "lint-rule008-009" ;
